**Blocked — Test how robust the profile-shape-driven bias evolution is to the emulator's astrophysical (feedback) and cosmological parameters. Estimate the non-thermal pressure fraction needed to reconcile M_HSE with the true mass..** (The tool budget ran out before I could load the 8 prediction CSVs and compute the finite-difference slopes and HSE ratios. The next step is to run load_table_data and the slope calculation on the d03_epskin_lo/ and d03_epskin_hi/ files.) Partly done. The predictions and comparison plots for the feedback test exist, but I did not read the numbers out of them, so none of the slope or mass results asked for are available yet. The feedback lever I chose is eps_kin (kinetic AGN feedback efficiency), whose allowed range is 0.02 to 1.2 (tc-...-61). This is a judgement call: the emulator does not say which parameter controls the density slopes. The other parameters stayed at the midpoints used in d-01 (kappa_w=3, e_w=0.6, M_seed=1.3, v_kin=0.65, omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). At the low and high eps_kin values I ran 8 predict_observable calls, CGD and CTP at z=0 and z=0.4987 (tc-...-71 to -78). The CSVs are in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-combo-cluster-profiles/runs/261020_143128/d03_epskin_lo/ and /d03_epskin_hi/. Two overlay plots compare these 4 runs per observable with the d-01 midpoint profile (eps_kin=0.61, z=0): Figure 21 (d03_plots_cgd/CGD_comparison.png, tc-...-81) and Figure 22 (d03_plots_ctp/CTP_comparison.png, tc-...-82). I did not run fGas. I did not work out the slopes s_n+s_T at R500c, T/T500, or M_HSE/M500 for the feedback runs, so I cannot yet say whether feedback changes the slopes more or less than redshift does. For the same reason I have no required non-thermal fraction to compare with X-COP (about 6% at R500) or with Nelson et al. As a reference point only, d-01's midpoint values (M_HSE/M500 = 0.925 at z=0 and 0.840 at z=0.4987) would need f_nth(R500c) of about 7.5% and 16% to give b=0, using f_nth ≈ 1 - M_HSE/M500. These are not feedback results. Posted finding f-008 and question q-08, which records the remaining work.
