[tool] d-05 post_finding {"claim": "I checked the pressure slope from CPP (P/P500, midpoint parameters) against s_n+s_T from CGD and CTP, using centred finite differences with the same 
[finding] f-012 I checked the pressure slope from CPP (P/P500, midpoint parameters) against s_n+s_T from CGD and CTP, using centred finite differences with the same bin pairs a
**Finding:** I checked the pressure slope from CPP (P/P500, midpoint parameters) against s_n+s_T from CGD and CTP, using centred finite differences with the same bin pairs and independent GP errors. At R500 they agree within 0.4 sigma. At 0.49 R500 they differ by 1.3 sigma (z=0) and 2.4 sigma (z=0.4987). At 2.05 R500 they disagree strongly, by 14 sigma (z=0) and 11 sigma (z=0.4987).

| Radius | z | s_P (CPP) | s_n+s_T | Difference |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.49 R500 | 0 | -1.981+-0.042 | -2.133+-0.104 | 1.3 sigma |
| 0.49 R500 | 0.4987 | -1.874+-0.088 | -2.218+-0.117 | 2.4 sigma |
| 1.00 R500 | 0 | -3.052+-0.113 | -3.128+-0.171 | 0.37 sigma |
| 1.00 R500 | 0.4987 | -3.232+-0.154 | -3.243+-0.172 | 0.05 sigma |
| 2.05 R500 | 0 | -2.877+-0.042 | -4.249+-0.086 | 14.4 sigma |
| 2.05 R500 | 0.4987 | -1.815+-0.207 | -4.463+-0.125 | 10.9 sigma |

So CPP is not the product of the CGD and CTP profiles at large radius.
